urnal": "J Leukoc Biol", "pages": "702-7", "pubMedIdentifier": 18070982, "volume": 83, "year": 2008, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18070982", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 450151, "displayName": "Distinct molecular mechanism for initiating TRAF6 signalling", "title": "Distinct molecular mechanism for initiating TRAF6 signalling", "journal": "Nature", "pages": "443-7", "pubMedIdentifier": 12140561, "volume": 418, "year": 2002, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12140561", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}], "species": [48887], "category": "binding", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}], "literatureReference": [165896], "relatedSpecies": [{"dbId": 181384, "displayName": "Chlamydia trachomatis", "name": ["Chlamydia trachomatis"], "taxId": "813", "crossReference": [{"dbId": 181385, "displayName": "NCBI_taxonomy:813", "databaseName": "NCBI Taxonomy", "identifier": "813", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/Browser/wwwtax.cgi?mode=Info&id=813", "className": "DatabaseIdentifier", "schemaClass": "DatabaseIdentifier"}], "abbreviation": "CTR", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}, {"dbId": 180800, "displayName": "Neisseria meningitidis serogroup B", "name": ["Neisseria meningitidis serogroup B"], "taxId": "491", "crossReference": [{"dbId": 180799, "displayName": "NCBI_taxonomy:491", "databaseName": "NCBI Taxonomy", "identifier": "491", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/Browser/wwwtax.cgi?mode=Info&id=491", "className": "DatabaseIdentifier", "schemaClass": "DatabaseIdentifier"}], "abbreviation": "NME", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "reviewed": [{"dbId": 1095192, "displayName": "Gillespie, ME, 2010-11-30", "dateTime": "2010-11-30 10:12:59", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}, {"dbId": 188961, "displayName": "Gay, NJ, 2006-04-24 16:48:17", "dateTime": "2006-04-24 20:48:17", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}, {"dbId": 2603254, "displayName": "Napetschnig, Johanna, 2012-11-16", "dateTime": "2012-11-16 19:43:52", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}], "species": [48887], "summation": [{"dbId": 2586632, "displayName": "Phosphorylation of IRAK-1 is due to three sequential phospho...", "text": "Phosphorylation of IRAK-1 is due to three sequential phosphorylation steps, which leads to full or hyper-phopshorylation of IRAK1. Under in vitro conditions these are all autophosphorylation events. First, Thr-209 is phosphorylated resulting in a conformational change of the kinase domain. Next, Thr-387 in the activation loop is phosphorylated, leading to full enzymatic activity. Several additional residues are phosphorylated in the proline-, serine-, and threonine-rich (ProST) region between the N-terminal death domain and kinase domain. Hyperphosphorylation of this region leads to dissociation of IRAK1 from the activated receptor complex. The kinase activity of IRAK1 is dispensable for IL1-induced NFkB and MAP kinase activation (Knop & Martin, 1999), unlike that of IRAK4 (Suzuki et al. 2002; Kozicak-Holbro et al. 2007), It has been suggested that IRAK1 primarily acts as an adaptor for TRAF6 (Conze et al. 2008).", "literatureReference": [165896, {"dbId": 450158, "displayName": "Lys63-linked polyubiquitination of IRAK-1 is required for interleukin-1 receptor- and toll-like receptor-mediated NF-kappaB activation", "title": "Lys63-linked polyubiquitination of IRAK-1 is required for interleukin-1 receptor- and toll-like receptor-mediated NF-kappaB activation", "journal": "Mol Cell Biol", "pages": "3538-47", "pubMedIdentifier": 18347055, "volume": 28, "year": 2008, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18347055", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 450177, "displayName": "Effects of IL-1 receptor-associated kinase (IRAK) expression on IL-1 signaling 